{"name":"Durian White","hex":"#e6d0ab","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"durian","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several trees, genus Durio, of Southeast Asia.","The spiky edible fruit of this tree, known for its strong taste and very strong, unpleasant odor."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/durian"},{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"}],"entries":[{"title":"Durian","blocks":[{"text":"The durian is the edible fruit of trees in the genus Durio, most often applying to those of Durio zibethinus, the only species available on the international market. Other species are sold in their local regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Durian_in_black.jpg/330px-Durian_in_black.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Durian","wikidata":"Q134185"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_co